  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Ashok Mangla vs State Of H.P on 1 August, 2019 Bench: Dharam Chand Chaudhary, Jyotsna Rewal Dua In The High Court Of Himachal Pradesh, Shimla. . Execution Petition No. 62 of 2019. Decided on: 1st August, 2019 Ashok Mangla ......Petitioner. Versus State of H.P. ....Respondent Coram The Hon'ble Mr. Justice Dharam Chand Chaudhary, Judge. The Hon'ble Mrs. Justice Jyotsna Rewal Dua, Judge.",
    "facts": "The complaint is that the respondent-State under the judgment sought to be executed required to fill up 14 posts of Designated Officers. The writ petition was disposed of while taking into consideration the reply filed by the respondent- State, as per which the process for filling up 10 posts was complete and qua remaining four vacancies, the process was to be initiated on creation thereof by the competent authority. The affidavit in compliance reveals that out of four, only two posts of Designated Officers were created by the Government vide notification dated 4.8.2015 and the same also stand filled up. However, only two posts have been created.",
